course: dictionary
lesson: 14765
title: Learning the word prosperity
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Prosperity is a noun. It means being successful and having plenty of money and good things. A family, a town or a whole country can have prosperity. «The village grew rich after the new bridge brought traders and jobs.» Now the village has prosperity, because it has money, work and good things.
explain: Prosperity often grows with trade, good jobs and good harvests. It falls in hard times, such as wars and recessions. «During the long war, the farms stood empty and the shops closed.» The clues show that prosperity was lost. Ask yourself: what would happen to prosperity if the harvest failed?
explain: People also wish each other prosperity. At Chinese New Year and Diwali, families share good wishes for luck and prosperity in the year ahead. Christians may pray for peace and prosperity. Phrases like «a time of prosperity» and «economic prosperity» help you spot the word when you read.
fact: Prosperity is a noun, and it is uncountable: we say «prosperity», not «a prosperity».
fact: «Prosperity» means being successful, with plenty of money and good things.
fact: A person, a town or a country can all have prosperity.
fact: Prosperity grows with trade, jobs and good harvests, and falls in wars and recessions.
fact: People wish each other prosperity at Chinese New Year and Diwali.
exercise: «The town enjoyed prosperity after the new harbour opened.» What does prosperity mean? | Being very quiet and calm | *Being successful, with plenty of money and good things | Losing all the money in the bank | Living in a small house
exercise: At Diwali, Priya's grandmother says, «I wish you health and prosperity in the new year.» What is she wishing for? | Rain for the garden | A new pet | *Success, money and good things | A long holiday from school
exercise: «The war brought hunger and an end to prosperity.» Find and copy the word that shows what the war took away. | hunger | war | *prosperity | brought
test: What does prosperity mean? | Being sad and alone | *Being successful, with plenty of money and good things | Plenty of money and good things | Being tired after a long walk
test: Which kind of event usually helps prosperity grow? | A long war | *Trade and good jobs | A recession
exam: In «a time of prosperity», what does prosperity mean? | A period of rain and storms | *A period when people have plenty and things go well | A period when the shops are closed | A period when everyone is cold and hungry
